{
  "dom_id": "step-q341608",
  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "Given that $x=-\\frac{2}{{y}^{2}}+5{y}^{2},$ express $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ as a function of $y.$\n\n| $\\text{d}y$ | $=$ | ${y}^{3}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{d}x$ |  | {{field-1}} |",
  "worked_solution": "First, we differentiate $x(y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(-\\frac{2}{{y}^{2}}+5{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(-2{y}^{-1}+5{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =-2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{-2})+5\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{2}) \\\\  & =-2(-2{y}^{-3})+5(2y) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{{y}^{3}}+10y \\\\  & =\\frac{4+10{y}^{4}}{{y}^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the reciprocal of $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{-1}=\\frac{{y}^{3}}{4+10{y}^{4}}.\n$$",
